ho desirest to see Him loved by all as He deserves.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":9,"label":"p. 9"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:14:1","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"8 INTRODUCTION. very moment in which it is satiating itselfwiththe utmost avidity; and when he had to do this, we are told that he remained standing with 1 his eyes cast on the altar, making repeated inclinations, as if he knew not how to quit his Lord, whose pre-~ sence was so sweet and gracious to him. §St. Aloy- sius was also forbidden to remain in the presence of _ ‘the Most Blessed Sacrament; and ashe used to pass before it, finding himself drawn, so to say, by the sweet attractions of his Lord, and almost forced — to remain there, he would, with ‘the greatest effort, tear himself away, saying, with an excess of tender love: Depart.from me, O Lord, depart! ‘There iit was also that St. Francis Xavier found refreshment in the midst of his many labors in India; for he — employed his days in toiling for souls, nud Ste!","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":14,"label":"p. 14"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:18:2","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Bernard is well known, and generally believed: it is, that God dispenses no graces otherwise than through the hands of Mary: ‘God wills that we should receive nothing which does not pass ‘through Mary’s hands’ Hence — Father Suarez declares that it is now the sentiment of the universal Church, that ‘the intercession of Mary isnot only useful, but even necessary toobtain i graces.’ And we may remark that the Church — gives us strong grounds for this belief, by applying 3 the words of the Sacred Scripture to Mary, and r, making her say: “In me is all hope of life and of virtue. Come over to me, all ye that desire me” (Ecclus. xxiv. 25). Let all come to me; for I am the hope of all that you can desire. pics then adds: ‘Blessed is the man that hearethae i and that watcheth daily at | gates, | ae","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":18,"label":"p. 18"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:23:3","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"ON SPIRITUAL COMMUNION. 17 -and at the same time nothing can he easier in practice. The above-named Blessed Jane of the Cross used to say, that a _ spiritual communion can be made without any one remarking it, without being fast- ing, without the permission of our director, and that we can make it at any time we please: an act of love does all. ACT FOR A SPIRITUAL COMMUNION, My Jesus, I believe that Thou art truly present in the Most Blessed Sacrament. I ~ love Thee above all things, and I desire to possess Thee within my soul. Since I am unable now to receive Thee sacramentally, come at least spiritually into my heart. I embrace Thee as being already there, and unite myself wholly to Thee; never permit _ me to be ed from Thee. A SHORTER ACT. I believe that Thou, O Jesus, art in the ~ Most Holy Sacrament! I love Thee and desire Thee!","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":23,"label":"p. 23"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:29:4","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"AND TO THE B. VIRGIN ‘MARY. 23 for ever, that henceforward no creature may enter there, to divide the love which is due to Thee, and which it is my ardent desire to bestow all on Thee. Do Thou alone, my dear Redeemer, rule me; do Thou ~ alone in full possess me; and if betimes I no not obey Thee periectly, chastise me with rigour, that thenceforward I may be more watchful to please Thee as Thou willest. Grant that I may no longer seek for any other pleasure than that of giving Thee pleasure; that all my pleasure may be to visit Thee often on Thine altars; to entertain myself with Thee, and to receive Thee in the Holy Communion. Let all who will, seek other treasures; the only treasure which Y love, the only one’ which I desire, is that of Thy love; for thisalone. will I ask at the foot of the altar.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":29,"label":"p. 29"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:33:5","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Now that I have found out Thy sovereign goodness, I haye become enamoured of Thee; I feel an ardent desire to love Thea and to please Thee; but I have not the strength to do this unless Thou helpest me. Manifest, O great Lord, Thy supreme _ power, and Thy immense gocdness to the | whole court of heaven; change me from a","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":33,"label":"p. 33"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:38:6","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"ENR S pe EA Se” Spl 0: 452 32 VISITS TO THE BLESSED SACRAMENI do on earth with the Most Blessed Sacra. ment.’ Behold, then, our'paradise on earth; —the Most Blessed Sacrament. O imma-~ culate Lamb, sacrificed for us upon the cross, remember that I am one of those souls which Thou hast redeemed by so many sufferings, and by Thy death. Grant that Thou mayest be mine, and that I may never lose Thee, since Thou hast given Thyself to me, and givest Thyself every day, sacri- ficing Thyself for my love on the altar ; and grant that I may be all Thine. I give myself to Thee without reserve, that Thou mayest dispose of me as Thou pleasest. I ' give Thee my will; chain it with the sweet bonds of Thy love, that it may for ever be the slave of Thy most holy will.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":38,"label":"p. 38"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:44:7","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"\\ ue ‘ 88 VISITS TO THE BLESSED SACRAMENT x my Jesus, who hast indeed done and suf. — fered great things for me! | _. EHjac. Grant, my Lord, that before J die, I may do something for Thee! Spiritual communion. VISIT TO MARY. ‘As a fair olive-tree in the plain.” Heclus, xxiv. 19. I am, says Mary, the beautiful olive. tree, from which the oil of mercy always flows. And I stand in the plain, that all may see me, and that all may have recourse to. me. ‘Remember (let us say in the words of the prayer of St.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":44,"label":"p. 44"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:49:8","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"AND TO THE B. VIRGINMARY. 43 and Infinite Goodness, and hast so tender% an affection for my soul! Ye souls who love God, wherever you may be, either in heaven or on earth, love Him foe me also. ° Mary, my Mother, help me to love Him. And Thou, most beloved Lord, make Thy- self the object of all my love. ‘Make Thy- self the Lord of my entire will; possess my entire self. -I consecrate my whole mind to Thee, that it may always be oe- cupied with the thought of Thy goodness; I also consecrate my body to Thee, that it may help me to please Thee; I consecrate my soul to Thee, that it may be all Thine. Would, O beloved of my soul, that all men could know the tenderness of the love © which Thou bearest them, that all might live only to honour Thee and to please Thee, as Thou desirest and deservest.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":49,"label":"p. 49"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:55:9","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"AND TO THE B. VIRGIN MARY. 51 Mary, if we would be rich in graces. The writer who calls himself‘the Idiot’ styles her ‘the treasure of graces.’ Blessed ig + he who has recourse to Mary with love and confidence. My Mother, my hope, thou canst make me a saint; from thee I hope for this favour.. jac. Mother most amiable, prayforme! | The usual prayer. Eleventh Visit. ‘Let us be careful,’ says St. Teresa, ‘never to be at a distance from, or to lose sight of, Jesus our beloved Shepherd; for the sheep which are near their shepherd are always more caressed and better fed, and always receive some choice morsels of that which he himself eats.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":55,"label":"p. 55"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:61:10","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Yes, my most amia- ble Redeemer,I will always love Thee; and Thou wilt always love me. I trust that our love will ever be mutual, O God of my soul, and this for all eternity. Amen. ac. My Jesus, I desire always to love Thee, and always to be beloved by Thee! Spiritual communion..","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":61,"label":"p. 61"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:66:11","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"and why have I Jost so many years, in which I have not loved Thee? O miserable years, I curse you; and I bless thee, O infinite patience of my God, for having for so many years _,borne with me, though so ungrateful to Thy love. And still, notwithstandin, this ingratitude, Thou waitest for me: and — why, my God, why? It is, that one day,— overcome by Thy mercies and by Thy — “9 ees te %,: any $i. | eect, 4,","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":66,"label":"p. 66"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:72:12","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"dress Thee in the words of the sisters of Lazarus: “ Behold, he whom Thou lovest is sick” (St. John xi. 3). Lord, I am that miserable creature whom Thou lovest; my soul is all wounded by the sins which | I have committed: my Divine Physician, I come to Thee, that Thou mayest a","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":72,"label":"p. 72"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:77:13","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"The usual prayer. i a ui : Stor Eighteenth Vist. = ==| One day Jesus will be seated on a throne _5 f majesty in the valley of Josaphat: but Ky aw, j Pants Se","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":77,"label":"p. 77"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:82:14","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"76 1 you alldays.” Behold Me, He says, all thine: I am come from heayen into thy \"prison expressly to console thee, to help _. thee, to deliver thee. Welcome Me, and do so always; cling to Me, and thus thou wilt never feel thy miseries; and afterwards thou wilt come with Me to My kingdom, where I shall make thee perfectly happy. -© God, O incomprehensible ocean of love, since Thy condescension towards us is so great, that in order to dwell near us - Thou descendest upon our altars, I propose often to visit Thee; I am determined, ag ~ often as I possibly can, to enjoy Thy most sweet Presence, which is the beatitude of the saints in heaven. Oh, could I but always remain in Thy Presence, to adore hee, and to make Thee acts of love! 3 Arouse, I beseech Thee, my soul, when through tepidity or worldly affairs it neglects to visit Thee.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":82,"label":"p. 82"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:88:15","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Twenty-First Visit, « Wheresoever the body shall be, thither will the eagles \\ also be gathered together,\"—St Luke xvii. 87. __ The Saints generally understand by this body that of Jesus Christ; and by the eagles, souls who, being detached from _ ereatures, rise above the things of the earth, and fly towards heaven, after which they always sigh in thought and affection, -and where they constantly dwell. These - eagles also find their paradise on earth wherever they find Jesus in the Most Holy ‘Sacrament; so much so, indeed, that they ‘seem never to tire hovering around Him. If eagles, says St. Jerome, on scenting a | deal body go from afar to seek it, how much more should we run and fly to Jesus. in the Most Blessed Sacrament, as to the most delicious food of our hearts! Hence Saints in this valley of tears have always.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":88,"label":"p. 88"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:93:16","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"I may again lose — Him. But thou canst obtain me ali; and from thee I hope for every good, for for-— iveness, perseverance,and heaven. [hope ) one of those 8. |in the emede ys of","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":93,"label":"p. 93"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:98:17","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"And what gratitude do they show Thee — in return, O great Son of God? QO Jesus, O too great Lover of men, allow me so to say, for I see that Thou preferest _ their advantage to Thine own glory. And —didst Thou not know to how much con-— tempt this loving design of Thine would expose Thee? I see, and before me Thou iA","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":98,"label":"p. 98"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:103:18","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"AND TO THE B. VIRGIN MARY, 97 ment in our churches to the Eternal Fa- ther. I know that on this altar Thou still lovest me with that same love with which Thou didst love me when Thou didst close Thy Divine life in the midst of so much anguish on the cross. O Divine Heart, enlighten all those who know Thee not with the knowledge of Thyself! Through Thy merits deliver from, or at least relieve, the pains of the afflicted souls in purgatory, who are already Thy spouses for all eternity. I adore Thee, I thank Thee, I love Thee, in anion with all souls who in this moment love Thee, be they on earth or in heaven, _O most pure Heart, purify my heart from all attachment to creatures, and fill it with Thy holy love!","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":103,"label":"p. 103"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:107:19","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Thou, O Sa- _ eramental Jesus, hast to be my comfort ,my \" love in life, and at the hour of my death, ' when Thou wilt come to be my Viaticum | and my guide to Thy blessed kingdom. ree amen. So do Lhope; so may “it be! . fac. When, O my Jesus, shall I “behold d Thy beautiful face! Spiritual communion, ti]","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":107,"label":"p. 107"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:112:20","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Let us, then,ever _ thank the goodness, the mercy, the liberal. | ity of our most loving God, who has been","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":112,"label":"p. 112"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:117:21","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Oh, what abundant fruits of virtues do those happy souls, like olive-plants, bring forth to God, who assist with love before the sacred tabernacle! But I am ashamed to appear before Thee, O my Jesus, so n& ked and so devoid of all virtues. Thou hast commanded that all who approach the altar to honour Thee should present a gift; “Thou shalt not appear empty before Me” ~ (Bx. xxiii. 15)..What, then, amI to do? > Am I no more to appear before Thee? ©","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":117,"label":"p. 117"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:122:22","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"So I hope; so may it be in time d in eternity ! _Hjac. Who shall separate me from the ove of Christ ! 1 os. Spiritual communion.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":122,"label":"p. 122"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:127:23","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Blessed Amadeus says, that our most blessed Queen, Mary, is always in the Di-— vine presence, acting as our advocate, and ~ interposing with God by her prayers, which — are most powerful :‘ The most blessed Vir- gin stands before the face of her Creator,—ty interceding with her most powerful prayers for us. For,’ he adds, ‘she well sees our miseries and our dangers, and the most — clement and sweet Lady compassionates and — succours us with a mother’s love.’ Thou","locator":