,"text":"146 = aors For HOLY cComMUNION. words which he addressed to His disci- ples: “But Me you have not always with you.” It is not advisable, as many do, to begin to read immediately after Communion: it is then better to spend at least a short time in producing holy affections, and in conyers- ing with Jesus, who is then within us, and » in repeating many times words of tender- ness, or some feeling prayer. Jesus Christ repeated the same prayer in the garden three times: “And He prayed the third time, saying the self-same word” (St. Matt. xxvi. 44).","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":152,"label":"p. 152"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:157:29","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"I at the same time give Thee _ all the powers of my soul, and I will that — they shall be all Thine; my memory I _ will only use to recall to mind Thy bene-— fits and Thy love; my understanding I will only use to think of Thee, who always thinkest of my good; my will I will only — use to love Thee, my God, my All, and to will only that which thou willest. My most sweet Lord, I offer, then, and conse- crate to Thee this morning all that Iam and haye,—imy senses, my thoughts, my affec- tions, my desires, my pleasures, my inclima-— tions, my liberty, in a word, I place my uct whole body and soul in Thy hands. 3 Accept, O Infinite Majesty, the sacrifice_ ___ of she hitherto most ungrateful sinner Thou —","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":157,"label":"p. 157"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:163:30","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"‘IN [HE BLESSED SACRAMENT. 157 jome and unite Thyself to souls in thia most sweet Sacrament? Wast Thou in-_ deed obliged to suffer so bitter and igno-| minious a death? Oh, come then, without » delay, and unite Thyself to my soul also. ~ It was at one time Thy enemy by sin; but now Thou desirest to espouse it by Thy grace. Come, O Jesus, my Spouse, for » never more will I betray Thee; I am de- _ termined to be ever faithful to Thee. As @ loving spouse, my whole thought shall be to find out Thy pleasure. Tam determined to love Thee without reserve; I desire to be all Thine, my Jesus,—all, all, all. II. “ A bundle of myrrh is my Beloved to me; He shall abide between my breasts” (Cant. i. 12). The myrrh plant when ricked sends forth tears, and a healthful tor from the wounds.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":163,"label":"p. 163"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:167:31","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"As if He said: Consider, My beloved, that I have waited for thee all the night of the bad life thou hast led in the midst of dark-— ness and error. Behold now, instead of wth bias to chastise thee, I come in the lessed tt with My hair","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":167,"label":"p. 167"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:172:32","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"10). Our beloved Jesus is all white by His pu- rity, and all red by the flames of His Divine love. My spotless Lamb, all burn- ing with love for me, when shall I ma myself like to Thee, pure as Thou art, lily; burning with love of Thee as The u ce ‘ fe","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":172,"label":"p. 172"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:177:33","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"b bsp a3 Piatt yes. Wi dp Lean! IN THE BLESSED SACRAMENT. 171. Thee in the path of virtue, and be able to repose peacefully in Thy Divine will both in this life and in the next: “Tn peace, in the self-same I will sleep, and I will rest ” (Ps. iv. 9). XIV. “The King brought me into the cellar of wine, and set in order charity inme” (Cant. ii. 4). It is precisely by this cellar of wine that St. Bonaventure ‘understands the Holy Communion which introduces and then unites the soul to its Divine King, and gives it to taste that wine of love which destroys the desire of created things; infuses a well-regulated Jove, that is just towards itself, charitable towards its neighbour, supreme towards God, loving Him above all things, who above all things deserves to be loved.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":177,"label":"p. 177"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:182:34","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"But as long ag live, I am in danger of changing my will and betraying Thee, as I have done before: do Thouhelp me. Help me also, most holy _ Mary; have pity on me: thou who art the Mother of perseverance, obtain for me — ale Pile","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":182,"label":"p. 182"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:187:35","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"is): vas Bich! JN THE BLESSED SACRAMENT. [gi | that God takes of a soul that He wishes — to have to Himself. He carries it written — in His hands, so that He may never forget~ it, and says, that sooner would a mother— \" forget her own son than He a soul in grace: “And if she should forget, yet will I not forget thee” (ib. v. 15), “ And thy walls are always before My eyes.” His eyes are always open, to watch over that soul, so that its enemies do it notharm: “Thou — hast crowned us, as with a shield of Thy good-will” (Ps. v.18). Our good God. surrounds us with the protection of Hig good-will, wholly solicitous for our good , ‘and so He delivers us from all dangers. © Ah, my God! infinite goodness, who more than any other lovest me and desirest my — good, I abandon myself entirely to Thee. Should every other hope fail me, Thou wilt never fail me.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":187,"label":"p. 187"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:192:36","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Pepa) o% ve DEVOUT ASPIRATIONS, TO BE MADE BEFORE AND AFTER COMMUNION, Extracted from the Mss. of St. Francis of Salea BEFORE COMMUNION. O my true and perfect Love, what affec- tion is this that brings Thee to such a miserable thing as I? Come, yes come, de- sired of my heart; my soul sighs for Thee; I offer to Thee, O my God, this commu- nion, to satisfy the desire Thou hast to come and unite me to Thyself, my God, and my All. Oh, what awonder! A God _ descends from heaven for me, and hides His _ majesty under the vile clothing of the spe- cies of bread and wine! Oh, how true it is,my Lord, that having always loved Thine ~ own, Thou hast loved them especially at _ the end, when Thou didst institute this _ Divine Sacrament. -.O my God, Thou art goodness itself; how, then, is it possible that I can lova anything else but Thee?","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":192,"label":"p. 192"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:197:37","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"AFTER COMMUNION. 191 holy will, strength against my bad. habits, remission of my sins, and grace rever more tocommit them. Give mea thorough con- tempt for all things, so that I may love none other but Thee. Give me patience to suffer for Thy love all that may happen to me. I hope all from Thee. O most holy Virgin, my dear Mother, beg of Thy Son, by the love He bears thee, to grant me, for thy sake, all I ask. My God, and my only good, I am more _ pleased in Thy infinite perfections than if they were my own. I rejoice that nothing in the world can take them from Thee, or diminish them. Come, then, Thou art al- ways welcome; always perfect and infinite in Thy majesty, O my Jesus, my Love and my God. Come and make me all Thine.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":197,"label":"p. 197"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:201:38","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"O my Jesus, by that eternal love which Thou hast borne me, give me grace to love Thee during the short time that remains for me to live on this earth, that I may af- _ terwards love Thee eternally in heaven. O God of love, make me live only for Thee. When shall I be all Thine, as — _ Thou art all mine? When shall I die to love? Ido ~ myself, to live only for Thy not even know how to give myself to Thee","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":201,"label":"p. 201"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:207:39","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"MOST HOLY S4CRAMENT, 201 PETITIONS TO THE MOST HOLY SACRAMENT. O my Jesus, now that Thou, who art the true Life, art come to me, make me die to the world, to live only to Thee, my Re- _ deemer; by the flames of Thy love destroy in me all that is displeasing to Thee, and give me a true desire to gratify and please Thee in all things. Give me that true humility which shall make me love contempt and self-abjection, and take from me all ambition of putting — myself forward. Give me the spirit of mortification, that I may deny myself all those things that do not tend to Thy love, and may lovingly embrace that which is displeasing to the senses and to self-love. Give me a perfect resignation to Thy will, that I may accept in peace, pains, in- firmities, loss of friends or property, deso- lations, persecutions, and all that comes to me from Thy hand.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":207,"label":"p. 207"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:211:40","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Omy — _ Jesus, would that I had died and never offended Thee! O love of my Jesus, Thou art my love and my hope! I will rather _ lose my life, and a thousand lives, than lose Thy grace. es My God, if I were to die in sin, I could ro more love Thee. I thank Thee that ‘ ) et ioe","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":211,"label":"p. 211"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:216:41","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"Jesus Christ answers, It is enough that it becomes My love. They feel great tenderness and devotion who go to Jerusalem and visit the cave where the Incarnate Word was born, the hall where He was scourged, the hill of Calvary on which ‘He died, and the sepul- _ehre where He was buried ; but how much greater ought not our tenderness to be when _ we visit an altar on which Jesus remaing —","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":216,"label":"p. 216"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:222:42","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"wit) = 216 MEDITATIONS FOR THE in the midst of a sea of ignominies and torments, in order to prove to us the affec- tion that He bore us; but besides all this in order to oblige us to love Him more, on the night before His death He would leave as His whole Self as our food in the Holy Eucharist. God is omnipotent; but after He has given Himself to a soul in this Sac- rament of love, He has nothing more to give her. The Council of Trent says, that Jesus, in giving Himself to usin the Holy Communion, pours forth, as it were, all the riches of His infinite love in this gift; ‘He has, as it were, poured forth the treasures of His love towards man.’ How would that vassal esteem himself honoured, writes St.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":222,"label":"p. 222"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:226:43","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"O beloved — One of my soul, would that I had alwaya loved Thee! Alas, there wasa time when _ J not only did not love Thee, but despised Thy grace and Thy love! Tam consoled i as","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":226,"label":"p. 226"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:231:44","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"COTAVE OF CORPUS CHRISTI. 225 MEDITATION VI. OS THE DESIRE WHICH JESUS CHRIST HAS TO UNITE HIMSELF TO US IN THE HOLY COMMUNION, “Jesus knowing that His hour was come (St. John xiii. 1). This hour, which Je sus called ‘His hour,’ was the hour of that “night in which His Passion was to begin- But why did He call so sad an hour His hour? Because this was the hour for which He had sighed during His whole life, having determined to leave us in this night the Holy Communion, by which He desired to unite Himself entirely with the souls whom He loved, and for whom He was soon to give His Blood and His Life. Behold how He spoke on that night to His disciples: “With desire have I de- sired to eat this Pasch with you.” By which words He would express ‘to us the desire and anxiety that He had to unite Himself with us in this Sacrament of love.","locator":{"kind":"pdf","page":231,"label":"p. 231"}},{"id":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf:pdf:236:45","bookId":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","filename":"Visits_to_the_Most_Holy_Sacrament-Liguori.pdf","type":"pdf","title":"Visits to the Most Holy Sacrament and to Most Holy Mary","author":"St. Alphonsus Liguori","text":"FOR THE f 230 MEDITATIONS Eucharist from mitted, and by the Holy Therefore ~ sins which we might commit, sinners must — St. Bonaventure says, that because not keep away from Communion on the contrary, — they have been sinners; ought to receive for this very reason they ‘the more — it more frequently; because